# Open in Rider or Visual Studio and run the requests one by one. Watch X-Elapsed-Ms in each response.
@host = http://localhost:5080

### 0. Restore seed data and invalidate earlier product/list caches (Development only)
POST {{host}}/demo/reset

### 1. The first call queries the "database" (about 300 ms)
GET {{host}}/products/1

### 2. The same call again comes from the cache (about 1 ms)
GET {{host}}/products/1

### 3. Another product, now cached as well
GET {{host}}/products/2

### 4. A cached list
GET {{host}}/products?category=keyboards

### 5. Change a price: invalidates product 1 and the lists, nothing else
PUT {{host}}/products/1/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 119 }

### 6. Product 1 is loaded again, with the new price
GET {{host}}/products/1

### 7. Product 2 is still cached (about 1 ms)
GET {{host}}/products/2

### 8. Hits, misses and entries
GET {{host}}/methodcache/stats

### 9. What is cached right now
GET {{host}}/methodcache/entries

### 10. Every cached method's policy and where each value came from
GET {{host}}/methodcache/methods

### 11. Invalidate by tag from the outside
POST {{host}}/methodcache/invalidate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tags": ["products"] }

### 12. Health check
GET {{host}}/health

### 13. Actual database reads on this instance
GET {{host}}/demo/queries
